new file mode 100644
index 0000000..948bfd8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/NOTES.md
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+# Discounts: notes
+
+Everything the docs settle I followed as written: discounts come off before tax and tax stays per line (ADR-0003, ADR-0006), they apply in the listed order, percent discounts are rounded per line with `round_cents` (ADR-0002), nothing goes below zero, each discount is its own row in the printed and the emailed invoice, issued invoices without discount fields still print and export (ADR-0004), and the CSV keeps its columns with `subtotal + tax = total` (ADR-0005). The document and computed field names are the ones in `docs/invoice-format.md`.
+
+## A decision I had to make
+
+**How a fixed discount is spread over the lines.** The docs say a fixed discount takes exactly its amount off the invoice (or what is left), but tax is per line, the computed form needs a `discount_cents` per line, and nothing says which lines it lands on. With mixed tax rates the answer changes the tax by a few cents, so it is not cosmetic.
+
+I spread it in proportion to each line's net at that point (`calc.spread_fixed`), giving leftover cents to the largest fractional share, earlier line first. Reasons: the shares add up to the amount to the cent, no share exceeds its line, it does not depend on line order, and every line's tax falls by about the same percentage. The alternative, taking it off the first line until that is used up, is simpler but makes tax depend on which line comes first.
+
+If product prefers another rule, only `spread_fixed` changes.
+
+Percent discounts are not affected: they apply to each line separately.
